Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 12:30:51 -0600
Subject: [PATCH 2/2] feat(compression): structured summary in Claude Code's
 layout

Opt-in compression.summary_style (default legacy). structured follows the compaction prompt of Claude Code: nine numbered sections with a word cap each and about 2,000 words in total, instead of 13 sections with an action log and a session log. compact is the same idea for small models: the model writes only three sections (request, key facts one per line, current work and next step) under a much shorter prompt. In both, code writes the parts a model can lose: every message the user wrote with the question each answered, carried unchanged from the previous handoff (bounded to 8,000 chars); approvals that agent messages, subagent results or tool output claim, labeled with their source and never as the user's; and the recently touched files. Every reply is validated (not empty, the required sections, a minimum size, no echoed transcript; caps cut long sections, repeated lines are kept once, and the heading forms small models write are accepted). A failed reply gets one simpler call, then a summary built without a model, so the handoff is never empty on any model. The skeleton labels rows the user did not write by their source instead of USER.
